Lobby
This is the pleasantly airy and open lobby of the building where all the executives keep their offices. A corridor leads visitors and executives north. The main campus is to the south.

There's a receptionist here, hunched over a computer and looking very bored.

>s

Campus Central
This central plaza is wide and spacious, offering striking views of all the major landmarks of the campus, as if designed by a brutalist landscape gardener.

As a wooden signpost indicates, the black glass building to the immediate north is the corporate headquarters; it also tells you that the campus stretches east to the engineering laboratory, and west to the customer service office. You can also leave the campus through the southern exit.

>e

Campus East
This part of the campus plaza wants to be open and airy, but it's hemmed in by various concrete structures, the biggest of them being the Engineering Laboratory to the north. Prettier parts of the campus are to the west.

Water cuts across the laboratory doorway here, spouting from a burst pipe in the wall.

There's a worker here, maybe a janitor or other maintenance person, leaning against the wall and holding a sign that says "VAMPIRES SUCK". There's just no need for that kind of tone.

>x water
A stream of water issues from a tear in one of the pipes in the wall. It's only a stream, but it's still running water.

>x worker
She's leaning against the wall, holding a protest sign. She spots you looking at her, nods at you and waggles the sign a little.

>talk to her
She nods at you as you approach. "Hiya. Vampires suck."

[1] What's the protest for?
[2] Could you fix this water leak so I can get to the laboratory?
[3] I'm trying to break into Hadrian Alba's computer. Do you know what his password is?
[4] Goodbye.

>1
"It's against vampires. Especially our guy in charge. It's against vampiric systems. It's against the exploitation of labour on long hours and low pay. It's for changes at the highest level for Lunarcel and every other company which lines its own pockets at the expense of workers. It's for radical new ways of being which aren't built on blood and toil." (You don't like this woman.)

[1] Isn't anyone else striking with you?
[2] But haven't vampires done so much for us?
[3] Could you fix this water leak so I can get to the laboratory?
