>1
"Hm? Oh, this?" The janitor glances at the rip in the water pipe next to her, as if she forgot about it. "Yeah, it's a nasty one. Don't know how it got there. Sorry, mate, I'm leaving it for now. Not much of a strike if I'm working during it. Can't you just cross it?" Before you can think of an excuse, she gasps. "Oh! Holes in your shoes? Fair enough, mate. Nice umbrella, by the way."

She thinks a little. "Tell you what, mate, can you do me a favour? I brought some raisins to snack on, but I think I left them in the prayer room. Can you get them for me? I'll tape up the leak for you when you do."

